# Recovery Tool — UI: ACP nachahmen

## Wenn `acp/style/style.css` geladen ist (`recoveryUsesNativeAcpUi()`)

**Nur WoltLab-ACP-Markup + `recovery-acp-native.css` (~150 Zeilen). Kein `recovery-acp-extensions.css`.**

| Element | ACP-Markup |
|---------|------------|
| Seitentitel | `contentHeader` + `contentTitle` (Layout) |
| Navigation | `nav.tabMenu` + `breadcrumb` |
| Abschnitt | `section.section` + `sectionHeader` + `sectionTitle` + `sectionDescription` |
| Tabelle | `table.table.tableList` — `recoveryAcpTableClass()` |
| Hinweis | `div.info` / `div.warning` / `div.error` / `div.success` mit `<p>` innen — **kein** Block in `<p>` |
| Listen in Hinweisen | `<ol>` / `<ul>` **außerhalb** von `<p>` |
| Dashboard-Kacheln | `div.acpDashboard` + `a.acpDashboardBox` |
| Formular (Auth) | `form` + `dl`/`dt`/`dd` + `div.formSubmit` |
| Auth-Login-Shell | `body.acpAuthFlow` + `pageHeaderContainerIsLogin` |

**PHP-Helfer:** `recovery-src/lib/Recovery/Ui/RecoveryAcpMarkup.php`, `recoveryRenderAlert()`, `recoveryRenderAcpSectionStart()`.

## Legacy (nur WCFSetup / ohne kompiliertes ACP-CSS)

Custom-Primitives: `recovery-chip`, `recovery-panel`, `recovery-status-feed`, `recovery-acp-extensions.css`.

## Verboten im ACP-Modus

- `recovery-panel`, `recovery-chip-bar`, `recovery-intake-hero`, `recovery-content-banner`
- `<ol>` innerhalb von `<p class="error">`
- Inline `style=` in PHP
- Neues Custom-CSS statt ACP-Klassen

## Release

`./dev/validate-php-syntax.sh` → `./dev/build-release.sh X.Y.Z` → `./dev/publish-github-release.sh X.Y.Z`
